==Trivia==
*Sportsgirl Cat's Japanese name, Motoko, is a shortened version of the phrase "Motokousaiaite", meaning an ex-girlfriend/boyfriend.
**It could also be a reference to Japanese volleyball star [[wikipedia:Motoko Obayashi|Motoko Obayashi]], since Sportsgirl Cat is shown carrying a volleyball.
*The text on Sportsgirl and Wrestling Cats' uniforms is 巨神 (''Kyoshin''), meaning ''titan''.
*Wrestling Cat's Japanese name, Sahori, may be a reference to former freestyle wrestler [[wikipedia:Saori Yoshida|Saori Yoshida]].
*Wrestling Cat's Korean name, Jang Mi-nyang (장미냥), references Olympic weightlifting champion [[wikipedia:Jang Mi-ran|Jang mi-ran]] (장미란).
*She is based on the [[wikipedia:Glossary of anime and manga#yandere|yandere]] character archetype, especially so in her first form.
*Prior to [[Version 5.9 Update|Version 5.9]], Wrestling Cat was named Olympienne Cat.

